messages:
maria-gonzalez: quick question — Product wants to onboard Heap for analytics on the dashboard. Does Heap capture full URL query params by default? we need to avoid user ids/emails in URLs. cc @security-bot @raj-patil
security-bot: Automated note: please attach the vendor security questionnaire and DPA if this is external. See /vendor-requests for the template.
raj-patil: short answer: Heap's web SDK records document.location.href by default (so query strings included). We should NOT send raw querystrings containing identifiers. Options: use Heap's mask/selective capture features, sanitize URLs before tracking, or configure server-side ingestion to strip params. Also require DPA + SOC2 review.
maria-gonzalez: thanks. We're planning pageview + product events only (no session replay). Elaine — any config suggestions from analytics side?
elaine-chen: we can do sanitize on the client and populate a redacted_url prop. example snippet below — it's what we've used for other trackers:
```js
function sanitizeUrl(url) {
  const u = new URL(url);
  u.search = ''; // drop querystring
  return u.pathname + u.hash;
}
window.addEventListener('load', () => {
  const safeUrl = sanitizeUrl(window.location.href);
  heap.track('pageview', { page: safeUrl });
});
```
raj-patil: 2 more things: (1) never call heap.identify() with an email or raw user id — use a pseudonymized id or hash, (2) restrict Heap access to analytics + product roles, no blanket org access. I'll need DPA + proof of SOC2 before final approval.
maria-gonzalez: got it. I'll start the vendor request and attach DPA when I have it. What retention window should we request?
elaine-chen: our default is 90 days for raw events, 13 months for aggregated. Security usually wants shorter; recommend requesting 90 days and export hooks for longer-term aggregated metrics.
raj-patil: agree — approval condition: (A) URL redaction implemented by client or ingestion; (B) DPA signed; (C) access scoped by role and logged. If those are met i'm good to approve. :white_check_mark:
security-bot: Approval workflow updated: vendor request 1769504321 moved to "pending docs". Please update the ticket with DPA link.
maria-gonzalez: tagging @jordan-smith to provision Heap access once docs are uploaded.
jordan-smith: got it — will create a permission group for "heap-analytics" with Just-In-Time membership, log RBAC in the vendor access register, and provision only after confirmation of DPA + redaction snippet.
maria-gonzalez: thanks everyone — i'll post the vendor request link here when submitted.
